; Bring a killed goblin back at its home
;
; Chained after the attack handler #R$9171 in the verb table of each of the six
; goblins (verb 0 = run after the previous entry). When the attacked character
; (Noun1Record) has just been killed (its dead flag, bit 3, is set) the goblin
; is revived: the flag is cleared, and the record found in #R$A49C by its id
; supplies the goblin's home. The id is stored back into the goblin's NPC
; state (so #R$980E runs it again; #R$977F had cleared it), and its location
; (+$10) and its second name phrase (+$0A, +$0B: it was replaced by the word
; "dead", #R$A18C) are restored. Prints "<goblin> falls down a hole and
; vanishes." and, when the player's location equals B, "Another goblin enters."
; So the goblins cannot be killed for good.
; .
; Hardware: none (the text goes through the message printer).
;
; B Compared with the player's location; nothing here sets it (a leftover of
;   the command dispatcher: $0E when the mean goblin was killed with the
;   player at $36), so the "Another goblin enters." line is unreliable
@label=RespawnKilledGoblin
c$A448 LD IX,($B708)  ; IX = the attacked character
@isub=BIT FLAG_DEAD,(IX+$07)
 $A44C BIT 3,(IX+$07) ; killed?
 $A450 RET Z          ; no: nothing to do
@isub=RES FLAG_DEAD,(IX+$07)
 $A451 RES 3,(IX+$07) ; alive again
@isub=LD DE,RESPAWN_RECORD_SIZE
 $A455 LD DE,$0006
 $A458 LD IY,$A49C    ; IY = RecordTable
 $A45C LD A,($B6E8)   ; A = the goblin's id
@label=RespawnKilledGoblin_Find
*$A45F CP (IY+$00)    ; find the record of that id (it is always there)
 $A462 JR Z,$A468
 $A464 ADD IY,DE
 $A466 JR $A45F
*$A468 PUSH IY
 $A46A POP HL
 $A46B INC HL
 $A46C LD E,(HL)
 $A46D INC HL
 $A46E LD D,(HL)
 $A46F LD (DE),A      ; the NPC state's id slot := the goblin's id
 $A470 INC HL
 $A471 LD A,(HL)
 $A472 LD (IX+$10),A  ; home location
 $A475 INC HL
 $A476 LD A,(HL)
 $A477 LD (IX+$0A),A  ; second name phrase restored (replaces "dead")
 $A47A INC HL
 $A47B LD A,(HL)
 $A47C LD (IX+$0B),A
 $A47F LD HL,$B068    ; "<obj1> falls down a hole and vanishes."
 $A482 CALL $72DD
 $A485 LD A,($C12B)   ; player's location
 $A488 CP B
 $A489 RET NZ         ; not equal to B: done
@isub=LD DE,WORD_ANOTHER
 $A48A LD DE,$005E
 $A48D CALL $74C1     ; "another"
@isub=LD DE,WORD_GOBLIN
 $A490 LD DE,$02E2
 $A493 CALL $74C1     ; "goblin"
 $A496 LD HL,$B018    ; "Enters."
 $A499 JP $72DD
